Chapter 10 – Dimension and Fact Tables

10.1 Overview

The Dimension and Fact tables form the business and analytical layer of the MHMR data processing solution in Microsoft Fabric.

After the source data is ingested and processed through the RAW, Staging, History, and Snapshot layers, business-specific transformation logic is applied to create the required Dimension and Fact tables.

The current implementation consists of:

15 Dimension Tables

3 Fact Tables

Unlike the common frameworks used for Staging, History, and Snapshot, each Dimension and Fact table has its own transformation code based on the corresponding business requirements and existing SQL implementation.

The objective is to reproduce the required SQL business logic in Microsoft Fabric while maintaining consistent data structures and expected results for downstream reporting and analytics.

