10.7 Validation

After the Dimension and Fact tables are loaded into Microsoft Fabric, validation is performed to ensure that the Fabric implementation produces the expected results.

The primary validation activities include:

Record Count Validation – Compare expected and actual record counts.

Source-to-Target Validation – Verify that required source data is correctly represented in the target.

Key Validation – Validate the required business and relationship keys.

Duplicate Validation – Identify unexpected duplicate records.

Null Validation – Validate mandatory and required attributes.

Transformation Validation – Verify calculated and derived columns.

Business Rule Validation – Confirm that required filters and conditions are correctly implemented.

Data Type Validation – Verify consistency of target data types.

Dimension/Fact Relationship Validation – Confirm required relationships between Fact and Dimension data.

Where applicable, the Fabric output is compared against the corresponding existing SQL results to verify that the migration maintains the expected business logic and data output.

10.8 Summary

The Dimension and Fact layer represents the final business-ready analytical layer of the MHMR Fabric solution.

The implementation currently consists of 15 Dimension tables and 3 Fact tables. Each table has its own transformation code based on the corresponding SQL implementation and business requirements.

Dimension tables provide descriptive and reference information, while Fact tables provide transactional and measurable business data.

The processing follows a common approach of selecting the required source data, applying joins and business transformations, mapping the results to the target structure, and loading the final tables into Microsoft Fabric.

Post-load validation ensures that the Fabric implementation maintains the required SQL business logic and produces the expected results for downstream reporting and analytics.
